# Complexity Comparison

| Solution                       | Time                                        | Space     |
| ------------------------------ | ------------------------------------------- | --------- |
| Brute Force                    | **O((n-k+1)² × k²)** (worst case **O(n⁴)**) | **O(1)**  |
| Prefix Sum (2D)                | **O(n²)**                                   | **O(n²)** |
| Sliding Window (1D Column Sum) | **O(n²)**                                   | **O(n)**  |

---

# Which Solution is Best?

* **Brute Force:** Easy to understand but far too slow for large `n`.
* **2D Prefix Sum:** Excellent when you need to answer many submatrix sum queries. It achieves `O(n²)` time but uses `O(n²)` extra space.
* **1D Column Sliding Window:** This is the most space-efficient solution. It also runs in `O(n²)` time while requiring only `O(n)` auxiliary space, making it the best choice for this problem.
